A change of mind mid-plan: mem holds the 2.0 docs plan (a migration guide, a
Close entry in the API reference and a screencast). The user calls off the
screencast and asks for the API reference. The screencast todo is dropped
with why, the reference is done and closed, and the guide stays open.

-- project/go.mod --
module db

go 1.22
-- project/db.go --
// Package db is a tiny database.
package db

// DB is an open database.
type DB struct{ path string }

// Open opens the database at path.
func Open(path string) (*DB, error) { return &DB{path}, nil }

// Close releases the database; using it after is an error.
func (d *DB) Close() error { return nil }
-- project/API.md --
# API

## Open(path string) (*DB, error)

Opens the database at path.
-- mem --
d := mem.Todo("ship the 2.0 docs")
d.Todo("write the migration guide")
d.Todo("document Close in API.md")
d.Todo("record a screencast of the upgrade")
-- prompt --
We're not doing the screencast for 2.0 after all, nobody watches them. Then go ahead with the API reference.
